      "writtenOn": "2026-02-05T22:34:19Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Question: Does webgpu not have a framebuffer-fetch-like functionality? DRLR would be needed for that too, if it does.",
      "revId": "abbcbf94a1d3e9ee8c789632f83b931a13d37c1e",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "b47e1f0f_3b48a298",
        "filename": "src/dawn/native/vulkan/PhysicalDeviceVk.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 953,
      "author": {
        "id": 1002296
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-02-05T22:35:48Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "In particular, the reason I\u0027m asking is that the barrier you have after unresolve says \"`dstAccessMask \u003d VK_ACCESS_INPUT_ATTACHMENT_READ_BIT`\", but if framebuffer fetch doesn\u0027t exist, that could have been `VK_ACCESS_COLOR_ATTACHMENT_WRITE_BIT`. And if it does exist, then you needed DRLR all along.",
      "parentUuid": "203f7239_e2e78329",
      "revId": "abbcbf94a1d3e9ee8c789632f83b931a13d37c1e",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "e0864e19_07b959c2",
        "filename": "src/dawn/native/vulkan/PhysicalDeviceVk.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 953,
      "author": {
        "id": 1004831
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-02-06T15:57:17Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Well WebGPU doesn\u0027t FramebufferFetch right now but it was added as a [Dawn/Tint extension](https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:third_party/dawn/docs/tint/extensions/chromium_experimental_framebuffer_fetch.md;l\u003d3?q\u003dtint%2Fextensions%2Fchromium_experimental_framebuffer_fetch.md\u0026sq\u003dpackage) for use by Graphite. Currently only Dawn/Metal supports the extension.\n\nI\u0027m currently working on the implementation for Dawn/Vulkan but was looking at non-dynamic rendering case first.",
      "parentUuid": "b47e1f0f_3b48a298",
      "revId": "abbcbf94a1d3e9ee8c789632f83b931a13d37c1e",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "3a09f8a6_a311aebc",
        "filename": "src/dawn/native/vulkan/PhysicalDeviceVk.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 957,
      "author": {
        "id": 1004831
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-02-06T18:46:09Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It does appear that VK_EXT_multisampled_render_to_single_sampled is more widely supported than VK_KHR_dynamic_rendering_local_read FWIW. Although Pixel 6+ supports both extensions.\n\n* [VK_KHR_dynamic_rendering](https://vulkan.gpuinfo.org/displayextensiondetail.php?extension\u003dVK_KHR_dynamic_rendering) is supported on 26% of Android devices\n* [VK_KHR_dynamic_rendering_local_read](https://vulkan.gpuinfo.org/displayextensiondetail.php?extension\u003dVK_KHR_dynamic_rendering_local_read) is supported on 9% of Android devices\n* [VK_EXT_multisampled_render_to_single_sampled](https://vulkan.gpuinfo.org/displayextensiondetail.php?extension\u003dVK_EXT_multisampled_render_to_single_sampled) is supported on 19% of Android devices",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 957,
        "startChar": 67,
        "endLine": 957,
        "endChar": 79
      },
      "revId": "abbcbf94a1d3e9ee8c789632f83b931a13d37c1e",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
